From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:46:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nfs/mount: define get_addr() and get_the_addr() as they are
 declared

Both are forward-declared with `rpcprog_t`/`rpcvers_t` at the top of mount.c
and then defined taking `ulong_t`:

    static struct netbuf *get_addr(char *, rpcprog_t, rpcvers_t, ...);
    ...
    get_addr(char *hostname, ulong_t prog, ulong_t vers, ...)

Whether that is a conflict depends on the data model, which is why it has
never been noticed:

    #if defined(_LP64)
    typedef uint32_t rpcprog_t;          /* four bytes */
    #else
    typedef unsigned long rpcprog_t;     /* == ulong_t */
    #endif

cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount has no amd64 subdirectory, so upstream builds it 32-bit,
where `rpcprog_t` really is `ulong_t` and the two spellings agree. Built
64-bit they disagree -- four bytes against eight -- and a compiler that
enforces it says so:

    error: conflicting types for 'get_the_addr'; have
        'struct netbuf *(char *, ulong_t, ulong_t, ...)'

Take the declarations as correct, since they use the types the RPC interfaces
actually specify, and make the definitions match. No functional change in the
32-bit build, where the types are identical.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 usr/src/cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount/mount.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount/mount.c b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount/mount.c
index efb1f998f3..391ca7d876 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount/mount.c
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/fs.d/nfs/mount/mount.c
@@ -1390,7 +1390,7 @@ make_secure(struct nfs_args *args, char *hostname, struct netconfig *nconf,
  * This is a potential routine to move to ../lib for common usage.
  */
 static struct netbuf *
-get_the_addr(char *hostname, ulong_t prog, ulong_t vers,
+get_the_addr(char *hostname, rpcprog_t prog, rpcvers_t vers,
 	struct netconfig *nconf, ushort_t port, struct t_info *tinfo,
 	caddr_t *fhp, bool_t get_pubfh, char *fspath, err_ret_t *error)
 {
@@ -1748,7 +1748,7 @@ check_nconf(struct netconfig *nconf, int nthtry, int *valid_proto)
  *
  */
 static struct netbuf *
-get_addr(char *hostname, ulong_t prog, ulong_t vers, struct netconfig **nconfp,
+get_addr(char *hostname, rpcprog_t prog, rpcvers_t vers, struct netconfig **nconfp,
 	char *proto, ushort_t port, struct t_info *tinfo, caddr_t *fhp,
 	bool_t get_pubfh, char *fspath, err_ret_t *error)
 {
